  "claims": [
    "Generic Four groupoid cancellation, square inversion and single-step-to-track naturality are derived operations, not new whole-track generators.",
    "Four typed internal wire frames have actual mixed placement and fusion edges. Their old/cartesian single-step naturality uses the existing eight fusion local forms.",
    "Naturality for an arbitrary cartesian proof track is recursively generated using only those step squares and groupoid operations, with empty guard support.",
    "The new definition basis extends the prior unified partial basis by Rewrite.Root-only definition generators: the eleven context-free old wire forms. It does not include the previous contextual-definition basis.",
    "Internal-context lifting of any old wire Step is derived using fusion square pasting, mixed whiskering, common-prefix cancellation and unit laws. No contextual old Step is a new definition generator.",
    "Every derived internal comparison has empty support and uses exactly one of the newly added context-free definition roots, independent of context depth.",
    "Whole mixed Steps/Tracks are eliminated using this root-only basis, preserving exact guard sets. The number of new definition-root uses equals the old-wire primitive usage count in the input track.",
    "Existing prior higher comparisons transfer compositionally to expanded boundary tracks with exact support; their new definition-root usage is the sum of the two boundary old-wire usage counts.",
    "The unchanged first-level mapper retains the previously proved zero legacy-label result and factor-twenty rewrite-use bound.",
    "Updated checked-model repair retains arbitrary correlated past and original shared state/input."
  ],
  "basis_contract": {
    "new_definition_argument": "Rewrite.Root only, eleven parameterized context-free forms",
    "prior_basis": "StatefulWiring.basis (before contextual wire-definition extension)",
