  "limits": [
    "This is relative to the existing parameterized old/cartesian one-step fusion naturality families, which retain actual typed wire-step/context payload. It is not a complete root-only presentation of every prior generator or all internal cartesian critical pairs.",
    "There are eleven new definition forms but infinitely many typed parameter instances; arbitrary wire/context/boundary data is not bounded by that count.",
    "One new definition use is not one total higher constructor: the concrete four-frame proof has 2793 constructors, excluding payload. No size or speed advantage is inferred.",
    "The first-level factor twenty counts rewrite occurrences including inverse uses, not total proof constructors, bytes, costs or forward simulation.",
    "Expanded boundary tracks are old-wire-free; the higher comparison internals may still retain prior-library generators. No projection of the entire higher basis or global higher conservativity/completeness is proved.",
    "The unified rewriting relation remains nonterminating under unrestricted expansion; remaining association/suffix/pure-wire overlaps and global finite coherence remain open.",
    "Stateful repair is endpoint equality inside an updated checked model. It does not automatically compare code-changing reductions, error budgets or full native/oracle-internal runtime.",
    "Ordinary shared proofs can use the same local constructions. Fair total-cost comparison and primary-theorem novelty are not settled."
  ],
